from your subsequent description you've just about completely eliminated
polymorph! that qualifies for "shutting down the _misuse_" but ...
well ... polymorph is a legitimate feature (as is wishing) ...
.
>   the polymorphing randomly destroys objects proposal
>   can be beaten by sheer volume.
.
theoretically, yes, but where is one to get the 100 potions (etc.) to
start with? remember, under the present rules it is possible to generate
ever-increasingly more magic from a small sample of (choice) magic. if
there was a chance that the choice magic was itself disintegrated or
could not be player-made that would tend to eliminate the misuse without
eliminating the strategy altogether ...

you can (currently, pl6) simulate this effect (to a degree) for yourself
by "polypiling" and manually "kicking out" every 20th item (5% probability
of loss or every 10th item for 10% loss). you'll see that in a fair trial
you can still get goodies (okay!) but that you can't get carried away ...

still, if a polymorph demon were to appear (i.e. created in the bowels of
your too large polypile) it would require one move to grab you and then
you've been scrambled (along with your inventory). the demon would thus
disappear. there are obvious strategies for dealing with this which involve
their own risks but it would seem to be a fitting reward for someone who was
going polycrazy ... now what was that demons name??? "Dave" ... naahh ...

